    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1014">

                <pb facs="0883" n="767" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg767"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3427.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-29T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1912—7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 28, 10 p.m. Informally inquire whether or not continuance of
                    Associated Press service can be arranged. Investigate the general policy of the
                    Mexican Government in this matter. In view of the conservatism of Associated
                    Press dispatches there appears to be no reason why their service should be
                    stopped.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
